+# Kähler/DH lane: exact volume law and failure of the virtual-scalar criterion
+
+## Provenance and scope fence
+
+The observation that TNS variational classes carry a Kähler structure and
+that TDVP is the associated Hamiltonian flow originated with Tobias Osborne,
+who communicated it to Jutho Haegeman, who made it work.  This observation
+must not be stated in any paper without TJO's explicit sign-off.
+
+Everything here is companion-paper material.  It does not target the Letter,
+does not assert that true scattering dynamics preserves a variational family,
+and does not turn a moment-map function into a GNS charge operator.  In
+particular, the REFUTED row `M-INDEX-LA-strong` remains untouched.
+
+## Honest status
+
+`BA-DH` is proved here only in its exact two-dimensional primordial/product-
+kink form.  In that form the flat pushforward is a change-of-variables
+consequence of the moment-map identity, not an independent DH mechanism.  The
+volume fixes the conversion `2s` charge units per lattice translation; the
+unit charge lattice is supplied by D26(INT)/`M-INDEX-fin`, not by scattering.
+
+For `BA-MM-mps`, the geometric dichotomy “global moment map iff
+`[iota_{xi^sharp} varpi]=0`” is proved under the regularity repair stated
+below.  The proposed further equivalence with scalar `V_alpha` is refuted:
+its advertised orbit period is identically zero, and a finite-support `CP^1`
+junction family has a global moment map despite nonscalar virtual `V_theta`.
+
+## 1. Primordial Archimedes calculation
+
+### ⟨1⟩1. THEOREM (spin-`s` sphere)
+
+**ASSUME.**  A single spin `s in {1/2,1,3/2,...}` is represented by its
+coherent-state projective sphere, with the selected circle generated by
+`S^z`; D26(INT) fixes `2s in Z`.  Use the circle orientation for which the
+fundamental field is `xi^sharp=partial_phi`.
+
+**PROVE.**  The moment map is `mu=<S^z>=s cos(theta)`, the symplectic form is
+
+`varpi_s = s sin(theta) dtheta wedge dphi`,                         **(1.1)**
+
+and
+
+`d mu = iota_{partial_phi} varpi_s`.                               **(1.2)**
+
+Moreover `mu_*(varpi_s)=2pi 1_{[-s,s]}(u) du`, so the normalized
+Liouville density of `S^z` is uniform on `[-s,s]`, and
+
+`int_{S^2} varpi_s = 4pi s = 2pi (2s)`.                            **(1.3)**
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  In the affine coherent coordinate
+`w=tan(theta/2)e^{i phi}`, expansion in `S^z` weights gives the
+unnormalized norm `(1+|w|^2)^{2s}`.  Direct differentiation of its logarithm
+gives
+
+`i partial partialbar [2s log(1+|w|^2)]
+ = 2s i dw wedge dbar(w)/(1+|w|^2)^2
+ = s sin(theta)dtheta wedge dphi`.
+
+*Justification.*  Named computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, geometry route in
+`sphere_routes`; the allowed half-integral values of `s` are D26(INT).
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  The binomial weight distribution of that same coherent vector has
+mean `s cos(theta)`.  Hence
+`dmu=-s sin(theta)dtheta=iota_{partial_phi}varpi_s`.
+
+*Justification.*  Named computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, observable route
+in `sphere_routes`, evaluated independently of the norm-Hessian route.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  On the open polar chart,
+`varpi_s=-dmu wedge dphi=dphi wedge dmu`.  Integrating the circle therefore
+gives pushforward density `2pi` on the moment interval.  Its total mass is
+`2pi(s-(-s))=2pi(2s)`.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩2 and named computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, gate G1.
+
+**⟨2⟩4.**  Dividing the Liouville measure by (1.3) gives density `1/(2s)` on
+`[-s,s]`.  Thus Archimedes' uniform-height law is exactly the DH pushforward
+in this two-dimensional case.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩3 and named computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, gate G1.
+
+**⟨2⟩5. QED.**
+
+### ⟨1⟩2. COROLLARY (what the volume does and does not quantize)
+
+**ASSUME.**  ⟨1⟩1 and the finite-window charge integrality of
+`M-INDEX-fin` under D26(INT).
+
+**PROVE.**  A symplectic flux of `2pi(2s)` corresponds to `2s` integral
+prequantum units.  Therefore one integral escaped-charge unit converts to a
+wall-position unit `1/(2s)`.  No scattering amplitude or channel probability
+enters this conversion.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  By ⟨1⟩1, the flux divided by `2pi` is `2s`.  By D26 and
+`M-INDEX-fin`, a fixed-window escaped-charge increment is integral after its
+common coset offset cancels.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩1, D26, and claim `M-INDEX-fin`.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  Charge balance converts an increment `nu` to
+`delta x=-nu/(2s)`; for `nu=1` its magnitude is `1/(2s)`.
+
+*Justification.*  D13(a), claim B3, and claim `M-INDEX-spec`.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  Geometry therefore fixes the conversion factor, while D26 fixes
+the charge lattice.  Geometry alone would allow a continuously rescaled
+moment map, and neither input determines the event weights `p_nu`.
+
+*Justification.*  D26 and the explicit conditional register of claim
+`M-INDEX-spec`.
+
+**⟨2⟩4. QED.**
+
+## 2. Exact D16/product-kink calculation
+
+### ⟨1⟩3. THEOREM (regularised Kähler cylinder and its period)
+
+**ASSUME.**  D16, `q=e^{-kappa}` with `kappa>0`, and its displayed
+coordinates `z=q^{-x_0}e^{i phi}`.  For the spin-`s` product generalization,
+use the same coherent tensor only as a variational family; exact ground-state
+status is asserted only at `s=1/2`, as frozen by D16.  Let `W=[a,b]`.
+
+**PROVE.**  The window curvature has the independent-sum form
+
+`varpi_W=Omega_W(x_0) dx_0 wedge dphi`,
+
+`Omega_W(x_0)=s kappa sum_{n=a}^b sech^2(kappa(x_0-n))>0`,           **(2.1)**
+
+and the D13(a) charge expectation satisfies
+
+`mu_W'(x_0)=-Omega_W(x_0)`.                                       **(2.2)**
+
+For the infinite exhaustion,
+
+`Omega(x_0)=s kappa sum_{n in Z} sech^2(kappa(x_0-n))`,             **(2.3)**
+
+and every lattice period has exact area
+
+`int_{x_0}^{x_0+1} int_0^{2pi} varpi = 2pi(2s)`.                   **(2.4)**
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  At site `n`, put `r_n=exp(kappa(x_0-n))`.  Pulling back the
+spin-sphere form of ⟨1⟩1 along `r_n=tan(theta_n/2)` gives
+
+`varpi_n=s kappa sech^2(kappa(x_0-n)) dx_0 wedge dphi`.
+
+The product-state Fubini--Study form is the sum of the local pullbacks, which
+is (2.1); each summand is positive.
+
+*Justification.*  D16 and named computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, geometry
+route `kink_routes`, gate G2.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  The local coherent-state expectation is
+
+`<S_n^z>=s(1-r_n^2)/(1+r_n^2)=-s tanh(kappa(x_0-n))`.
+
+The additive constants in `Qhat_{W,c_0}=2s(X_W-c_0)` disappear on
+differentiation, so summing
+`d<S_n^z>/dx_0=-s kappa sech^2(kappa(x_0-n))` proves (2.2).
+
+*Justification.*  D13(a), D16, and the independent observable route in named
+computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, gate G2.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  Equations (2.1)--(2.2) give
+`dmu_W=iota_{partial_phi}varpi_W`; hence the windowed D13(a) expectation is a
+moment map.  This is a function on the displayed family, not a GNS operator.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩1--⟨2⟩2, D13(a), and the REFUTED fence
+`M-INDEX-LA-strong`.
+
+**⟨2⟩4.**  For a symmetric finite window `[-L,L]`, the exact one-period
+integral is
+
+`int_x^{x+1} Omega_{[-L,L]}(t)dt
+ =s[tanh(kappa(x+L+1))-tanh(kappa(x-L))]`.                          **(2.5)**
+
+Thus it is not literally `2s` at finite `L`; the difference is the explicit
+edge term.  Taking `L to infinity` gives `2s`, independently of `x`, proving
+(2.4).
+
+*Justification.*  Telescoping the antiderivative of each term in (2.1);
+named computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, gate G3.
+
+**⟨2⟩5.**  The series (2.3) converges locally uniformly with all derivatives,
+is positive and one-periodic.  Consequently the limiting form is symplectic
+on the cylinder and its pushforward under `mu` has constant density `2pi`.
+
+*Justification.*  The `sech^2` summands and all derivatives decay
+exponentially in `|n|`; (2.2), D16, and named computation
+`check_kaehler_dh.py`, gates G2--G4.
+
+**⟨2⟩6.**  In the displayed D16 orientation, increasing `x_0` makes `mu`
+decrease, so `mu(x_0+1)-mu(x_0)=-2s`.  Reversing the wall orientation reverses
+this sign.  The invariant statement is `|Delta mu|=2s` and positive volume
+`2pi(2s)`.
+
+*Justification.*  (2.2)--(2.4) and D16's fixed `z=q^{-x_0}e^{i phi}`.
+
+**⟨2⟩7. QED.**
+
+### ⟨1⟩4. COROLLARY (sharp-kink staircase and flat pushforward)
+
+**ASSUME.**  ⟨1⟩3 and the sharp limit `kappa to infinity`.
+
+**PROVE.**  Distributionally,
+
+`Omega_kappa(x) dx -> 2s sum_{n in Z} delta_n(dx)`,                 **(2.6)**
+
+so `mu` tends to a staircase with jumps of magnitude `2s` at lattice sites
+and plateaus between them.  For every finite `kappa`, however, the Liouville
+pushforward is flat; the staircase is the moment map, not its DH density.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  Each bump
+`s kappa sech^2(kappa(x-n))` has mass `2s` and concentrates at `n`.
+
+*Justification.*  (2.1) and named computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, gate G3.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  Since `mu'=-Omega`, (2.6) integrates to downward steps of size
+`2s` in the D16 orientation.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩3 and ⟨2⟩1.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  Before the singular limit,
+`varpi=-dmu wedge dphi`, so pushforward along `mu` is exactly
+`2pi dmu`; no plateau appears in that density.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩3 and named computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, gate G1's
+independent strip check.
+
+**⟨2⟩4. QED.**
+
+### ⟨1⟩5. COROLLARY (corpus cross-check, with no fitting)
+
+**ASSUME.**  ⟨1⟩2--⟨1⟩3 and an escaped-charge outcome `nu=2`.
+
+**PROVE.**  `delta x=-nu/(2s)=-1/s`, which is exactly the conditional
+transmission outcome in `M-quant-G`, the `nu=2` member of `M-INDEX-spec`, and
+the magnitude of the `S2-2body-S` slope.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  Substitute `nu=2` in the conversion of ⟨1⟩2.
+
+*Justification.*  Claim `M-INDEX-spec`.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  Compare the result with the displayed conclusions of
+`M-quant-G` and `S2-2body-S`; no model parameter or scattering probability is
+fitted.
+
+*Justification.*  Claims `M-quant-G` and `S2-2body-S`.
+
+**⟨2⟩3. QED.**
+
+## 3. L2: what survives for regularised injective-MPS families
+
+### ⟨1⟩6. PROPOSITION (the genuine global dichotomy)
+
+**ASSUME.**  The L2 hypotheses from the target brief, with two explicit
+regularity readings: window forms and the circle action are smooth; and
+`(FS-conv)` means `C^1_loc` convergence of forms (or another hypothesis that
+guarantees a smooth closed limit).  Also assume the limiting form is
+nondegenerate where a symplectic conclusion is wanted.
+
+**PROVE.**  The limit `varpi` is closed and circle-invariant,
+`alpha_xi:=iota_{xi^sharp}varpi` is closed, and a global real moment map exists
+if and only if
+
+`[alpha_xi]=0 in H^1_dR(M)`.                                      **(3.1)**
+
+When it exists it is unique up to one constant on every connected component.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  The `(FS-conv)` Cauchy estimate makes every padded exhaustion have
+the same local limit.  The cut `c_0` does not enter the window Fubini--Study
+form, so the limiting form is cut-independent.
+
+*Justification.*  D1(e)--(e′), D1(c)'s honest `lambdatilde` discipline, and
+the stated strengthened reading of `(FS-conv)`.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  Since `dvarpi_W=0` and the convergence is `C^1_loc`, passing to the
+limit gives `dvarpi=0`.  Since each window pullback is invariant under the
+selected unitary circle action, passing to the limit gives
+`L_{xi^sharp}varpi=0`.
+
+*Justification.*  D2(a),(e), D1(e), and the stated strengthened
+`(FS-conv)` reading.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  Cartan's identity gives
+
+`d alpha_xi = d iota_{xi^sharp}varpi
+ = L_{xi^sharp}varpi-iota_{xi^sharp}dvarpi=0`.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩2 and named computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, gate G5's
+antisymmetry audit.
+
+**⟨2⟩4.**  A global moment map is precisely a function `mu_varpi` satisfying
+`dmu_varpi=alpha_xi`; such a function exists exactly when the closed form
+`alpha_xi` is exact, which is (3.1).
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩3 and the moment-map candidate type fixed by D13(a);
+no operator statement is used.
+
+**⟨2⟩5.**  If `mu_1` and `mu_2` both solve the equation, then
+`d(mu_1-mu_2)=0`, so their difference is constant on each connected
+component.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩4.
+
+**⟨2⟩6. QED.**
+
+### ⟨1⟩7. REGULARITY LIMIT (literal `(FS-conv)` is too weak)
+
+**ASSUME.**  `(FS-conv)` is read literally as only uniform `C^0` convergence
+of coefficient functions on compacta, as its proposed norm currently says.
+
+**PROVE.**  That hypothesis yields a continuous weakly closed limit, but does
+not by itself yield the smooth symplectic form required by L2.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  Stokes' identity passes through uniform convergence on every
+smooth compact chain, so the limit is closed in the distributional/integral
+sense.
+
+*Justification.*  The proposed `(FS-conv)` estimate and D1(c)'s uniform
+compact control.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  Uniform limits of smooth coefficient functions need not be
+differentiable, and nondegeneracy is not preserved without a uniform lower
+bound.  Therefore smoothness, Lie derivatives, and inversion to a Poisson
+tensor require extra hypotheses.
+
+*Justification.*  This is the standard elementary uniform-limit counterfact;
+the needed repair is independently exercised by named computation
+`check_kaehler_dh.py`, gate G4, only on the D16 instance.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  A viable repair is to require `C^1_loc` convergence plus a compact-
+local lower bound on the least symplectic singular value (or to formulate the
+limit as a continuous weak symplectic structure and postpone Poisson
+inversion).
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩1--⟨2⟩2.
+
+**⟨2⟩4. QED.**
+
+### ⟨1⟩8. NO-GO (the proposed `phi`-orbit period is always zero)
+
+**ASSUME.**  Any two-form `varpi`, any circle action with fundamental field
+`xi^sharp`, and an orbit `gamma(theta)=exp(theta xi)m`.
+
+**PROVE.**  The proposed D34(c) period along that orbit obeys
+
+`oint_gamma iota_{xi^sharp}varpi=0`,                               **(3.2)**
+
+whether `V_alpha(exp(theta xi))` is scalar or nonscalar.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  Along the orbit, `dot gamma=xi^sharp`.  Hence the integrand is
+
+`(iota_{xi^sharp}varpi)(dot gamma)=varpi(xi^sharp,xi^sharp)=0`
+
+pointwise by antisymmetry.
+
+*Justification.*  Named computation `check_kaehler_dh.py`, gate G5.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  Therefore a proposed P6 requiring this orbit period to be nonzero
+for nonscalar `V_theta` cannot pass if it computes the stated mathematical
+quantity.  A nonzero output would mean it computed a transverse cycle or a
+different one-form.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨2⟩1 and the scalar/nonscalar branch in claim
+`M-INDEX-LA-strong`'s second refutation mechanism.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  Exactness must instead be tested on all homology classes:
+`[alpha_xi]=0` iff `oint_gamma alpha_xi=0` for every closed one-cycle
+`[gamma] in H_1(M;R)`.  Relevant cycles are generally transverse to the
+circle orbits.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩6 and (3.2).
+
+**⟨2⟩4. QED.**
+
+### ⟨1⟩9. COUNTEREXAMPLE (`mu_varpi` exists with nonscalar `V_theta`)
+
+**ASSUME.**  The D23 AKLT tensor `B^a` and its spin-`1/2` virtual rotation
+`V_theta`, together with an auxiliary physical two-level charge doublet and
+`G=U(1) rtimes Z_2`, where the reflection flips both physical factors.  On
+one site take the selected charge
+
+`S^z_tot=diag(1,-1) tensor 1 + 1 tensor S^z_AKLT`.
+
+Let the two tail tensors be
+
+`A_alpha^{(sigma,a)}=delta_{sigma,up} B^a`,
+`A_beta ^{(sigma,a)}=delta_{sigma,down} B^a`,                       **(3.3)**
+
+and at the junction replace the auxiliary-qubit factor by a ray
+`[u_up:u_down] in CP^1`, leaving `B^a` unchanged.
+
+**PROVE.**  This is an L2 family satisfying `(FOL)` and `(FS-conv)`, its tail
+virtual circle is nonscalar, and its selected circle nevertheless has the
+global moment map
+
+`mu_varpi([u])=(|u_up|^2-|u_down|^2)/(|u_up|^2+|u_down|^2)`.         **(3.4)**
+
+Thus “moment map exists only if `V_theta` is scalar” is false.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  Each tensor in (3.3) has the AKLT transfer map, so it is injective
+with bond dimension `2`; the two states are distinct because their auxiliary
+qubit tails are opposite.  The diagonal `U(1)` leaves both states invariant,
+and the reflection that flips both physical spins exchanges the tails.
+
+*Justification.*  D1(b)--(d), D2(a), D23, and claim `SPT-E'`.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  The selected on-site spectrum is integral, so D26(INT) holds.
+The AKLT contribution has zero density and the auxiliary charge doublet
+contributes tail densities `+1` and `-1`; the D13(a) calibration is therefore
+`s=1`.
+
+*Justification.*  D23, D26, D13(a), and claim `M-IDX-density`'s explicit
+fence allowing non-fully-polarised injective tails.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  The family changes only the junction qubit.  Hence every member is
+a D1(e′) two-sided decoration in `K^{(1)}_{alpha beta}`, and any two members
+differ by a bounded local operation.  They are mutually normal, so `(FOL)`
+holds.
+
+*Justification.*  D1(e′), D17, and the definition of `(FOL)` in the target
+brief.
+
+**⟨2⟩4.**  Once a window contains the junction, its vector factorizes into
+the junction qubit ray and an AKLT window vector.  The AKLT norm contributes
+only a parameter-independent additive term to the window potential.
+Consequently the pulled-back curvature is the standard `CP^1` form for every
+such window: convergence is exact, hence `(FS-conv)` holds at every
+derivative order.
+
+*Justification.*  D1(e), D23, and the spin-`1/2` instance of ⟨1⟩1.
+
+**⟨2⟩5.**  The physical `U(1)` rotation of the AKLT factor is absorbed by its
+virtual symmetry, while on the junction ray it is the opposite-weight
+`(+1,-1)` circle action.  The standard `CP^1` curvature of ⟨1⟩1 with the
+twice-primitive fundamental field has the global moment map (3.4).
+
+*Justification.*  D2(b), D23, claim `SPT-E'`, and ⟨1⟩1.
+
+**⟨2⟩6.**  For generic `theta`, the AKLT virtual rotation has two distinct
+spin-`1/2` eigenvalues and is nonscalar.  Thus ⟨2⟩5 and nonscalarity coexist
+on the same family.
+
+*Justification.*  D23, claim `SPT-E'`, and named computation
+`check_kaehler_dh.py`, gate G5 (`V` scalar-distance `1` at `theta=pi/2`).
+
+**⟨2⟩7. QED.**
+
+### ⟨1⟩10. DECISION ON THE L2 PREDICTION
+
+**ASSUME.**  The exactness dichotomy of ⟨1⟩6, the orbit calculation ⟨1⟩8,
+and the counterexample ⟨1⟩9.
+
+**PROVE.**  The pre-registered equivalence
+
+`[iota_{xi^sharp}varpi]=0 iff V_alpha(exp(theta xi)) is scalar for all theta`
+
+is REFUTED at the generality of L2.
+
+**⟨2⟩1.**  The implication “exact moment map implies scalar `V_theta`” is
+false by ⟨1⟩9.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩9.
+
+**⟨2⟩2.**  The proposed proof route through the symmetry-orbit period cannot
+establish either implication because that period vanishes identically.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩8.
+
+**⟨2⟩3.**  The reverse implication “scalar `V_theta` implies exactness” does
+not follow from `(FS-conv)+(FOL)`: those hypotheses contain neither the full
+period data of `alpha_xi` nor convergence of the calibrated functions
+`mu_W`.  This direction remains open under an additional, explicit bridge.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩6, D13(a), and claim `M-INDEX-LA-strong`'s explicit note
+that even the operator-side scalar converse was not proved.
+
+**⟨2⟩4.**  A viable forward attack is to compute the flux class
+`Flux_xi=[iota_{xi^sharp}varpi]` on a basis of `H_1(M;R)` and separately
+construct a transgression/holonomy map from the virtual endpoint data to
+those transverse periods.  Any scalar-`V` criterion must be a theorem about
+that map, not about the orbit period.
+
+*Justification.*  ⟨1⟩6--⟨1⟩9 and D4's state-level virtual-action register.
+
+**⟨2⟩5. QED.**
+
